WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.561 --> 00:00:04.185
- We are back with Billy Ray
Cyrus, Firerose and Sam J.

00:00:04.185 --> 00:00:05.715
Give it up everybody.

00:00:05.715 --> 00:00:07.356
(crowd cheering)

00:00:07.356 --> 00:00:10.021
So last season we announced
that our partner Pilot Pen

00:00:10.021 --> 00:00:12.512
was searching for their next $100,000

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.475
G2 Overachievers grant winner.

00:00:14.475 --> 00:00:15.308
That is not a typo.

00:00:15.308 --> 00:00:16.803
That is a hundred grand y'all.

00:00:16.803 --> 00:00:19.757
There are some people out
there who go above and beyond

00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:21.120
to make our world a better place.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.233
Just walking around
here, just being angels.

00:00:23.233 --> 00:00:25.040
And that certainly
describes my next guest.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.492
Her organization helps
children in foster care

00:00:27.492 --> 00:00:29.054
find forever families.

00:00:29.054 --> 00:00:30.565
That's why Pilot selected her

00:00:30.565 --> 00:00:33.096
as a G2 Overachievers finalist

00:00:33.096 --> 00:00:34.633
and shared her story with us,

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:35.872
which we are so excited about.

00:00:35.872 --> 00:00:38.355
Please everybody welcome Marcy Bursac,

00:00:38.355 --> 00:00:41.121
along with Pilot's Vice
President of Marketing,

00:00:41.121 --> 00:00:42.299
Ariann Langsam.

00:00:42.299 --> 00:00:43.908
(audience cheering)

00:00:43.908 --> 00:00:45.364
So meet everybody.

00:00:45.364 --> 00:00:46.197
Hello!

00:00:47.895 --> 00:00:48.994
And Marcy, I'm gonna start with you.

00:00:48.994 --> 00:00:50.162
So explain to everybody,

00:00:50.162 --> 00:00:51.662
forgotten adoption option.

00:00:51.662 --> 00:00:52.642
- [Marcy] Kind of rolls
off the tongue, right?

00:00:52.642 --> 00:00:53.475
- It really does.

00:00:53.475 --> 00:00:54.308
It's very nice.

00:00:54.308 --> 00:00:55.270
Yeah, explain how it works.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:56.948
- Yeah so essentially I coach families

00:00:56.948 --> 00:00:58.214
through the adoption process.

00:00:58.214 --> 00:01:00.100
So many people are really familiar with

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.332
you can spend thousands of
dollars, tens of thousands,

00:01:02.332 --> 00:01:04.465
to adopt a child and it
takes a long process.

00:01:04.465 --> 00:01:06.184
Or you can become a foster parent

00:01:06.184 --> 00:01:08.927
and maybe you'll adopt
that child, but maybe not.

00:01:08.927 --> 00:01:09.760
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.476
- People often don't know
there's a third option,

00:01:11.476 --> 00:01:13.511
and that's why it's called
the forgotten adoption option.

00:01:13.511 --> 00:01:17.105
There are 30% of the children
currently in foster care

00:01:17.105 --> 00:01:18.940
are adoptable right now

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:20.415
and you can adopt them.

00:01:20.415 --> 00:01:22.407
And in fact, that process is shorter.

00:01:22.407 --> 00:01:25.882
The financial investment
is at maximum $2,500.

00:01:25.882 --> 00:01:27.378
The state often covers health insurance

00:01:27.378 --> 00:01:28.948
for these children until they're 18.

00:01:28.948 --> 00:01:29.781
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:29.781 --> 00:01:30.656
- So, that's really the organization.

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:32.638
- And they're forgotten sometimes,

00:01:32.638 --> 00:01:33.787
they're overlooked, right?

00:01:33.787 --> 00:01:34.719
- [Marcy] They're overlooked, yes.

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:36.445
- Because I had never
heard of this before you.

00:01:36.445 --> 00:01:37.278
- [Marcy] Now you have.

00:01:37.278 --> 00:01:38.217
- Had you heard of this before?

00:01:38.217 --> 00:01:39.896
I'd never heard of it.

00:01:39.896 --> 00:01:41.938
Yeah, so what stood out about-

00:01:41.938 --> 00:01:44.247
so many great organizations come across,

00:01:44.247 --> 00:01:45.380
you know, your desk.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.999
So what stood out about Marcy's?

00:01:46.999 --> 00:01:48.664
- Well, what really stood out about Marcy

00:01:48.664 --> 00:01:51.126
is that she is an incredible overachiever.

00:01:51.126 --> 00:01:53.793
She fits with the G2 paradigm that

00:01:53.793 --> 00:01:56.004
write more, do more, achieve more.

00:01:56.004 --> 00:01:57.322
And I'm not sure if you know this,

00:01:57.322 --> 00:02:00.720
but Marcy is a professional,
she's a technical analyst.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.763
She also recently finished her MBA.

00:02:02.763 --> 00:02:06.259
She has been a pageant
contestant and winner.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.101
She's written.

00:02:07.101 --> 00:02:07.934
- (snaps) Okay.

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:09.600
- Yeah, I know.
(Marcy laughing)

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:10.433
- Just all those little bullet points.

00:02:10.433 --> 00:02:11.822
- But there's more.

00:02:11.822 --> 00:02:12.772
Okay, so lemme keep going.

00:02:12.772 --> 00:02:14.954
So she has written two books.

00:02:14.954 --> 00:02:17.244
A third one is coming out very soon.

00:02:17.244 --> 00:02:20.436
She is a podcaster, she is a wife,

00:02:20.436 --> 00:02:23.996
she and her husband adopted
two children from foster care,

00:02:23.996 --> 00:02:27.240
and in her spare time, Marcy has helped

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.329
over 12,000 families through the process.

00:02:30.329 --> 00:02:32.505
(audience cheering)

00:02:32.505 --> 00:02:36.307
- How do you have spare
time in all of that?

00:02:36.307 --> 00:02:37.835
I'm like, what?

00:02:37.835 --> 00:02:39.536
Where is the spare time?

00:02:39.536 --> 00:02:41.548
- If I write a fourth book, it
might be on time management.

00:02:41.548 --> 00:02:42.381
- I know.

00:02:42.381 --> 00:02:45.045
I was like, yeah, I need
that book desperately.

00:02:45.045 --> 00:02:45.947
(Ariann laughing)

00:02:45.947 --> 00:02:47.553
So this work is very
personal to you, right?

00:02:47.553 --> 00:02:48.386
- [Marcy] It is.

00:02:48.386 --> 00:02:49.219
- Yeah.

00:02:49.219 --> 00:02:50.779
- Yeah, Kelly, when I
was in my early twenties

00:02:50.779 --> 00:02:53.260
I had the opportunity to
go on a service project

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.022
over to an orphanage in Europe.

00:02:55.022 --> 00:02:57.806
And I spent a good portion
of my week with teen girls.

00:02:57.806 --> 00:02:58.639
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:58.639 --> 00:02:59.472
- Who were in this orphanage.

00:02:59.472 --> 00:03:00.536
And it really hurt.

00:03:00.536 --> 00:03:02.904
Like, I just felt the
burden in my heart of,

00:03:02.904 --> 00:03:05.691
man, these kids, they're
growing up without a family.

00:03:05.691 --> 00:03:07.586
And they're not just growing
up in their childhood.

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:10.553
They're growing up with their
lifetime without a family.

00:03:10.553 --> 00:03:12.175
And when I came back to the US I thought,

00:03:12.175 --> 00:03:13.956
I'm not okay with what I saw

00:03:13.956 --> 00:03:15.523
and I need to do something about it.

00:03:15.523 --> 00:03:18.340
And so I decided, I'm going
to adopt as my plan A.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.803
And that's what my husband and I did.

00:03:19.803 --> 00:03:21.539
We actually adopted two kids together.

00:03:21.539 --> 00:03:23.053
They're biological siblings.

00:03:23.053 --> 00:03:24.308
- [Kelly] Yeah, oh, that's great!

00:03:24.308 --> 00:03:25.141
(audience cheering)

00:03:25.141 --> 00:03:26.566
Because it's good to keep
the siblings together.

00:03:26.566 --> 00:03:27.514
- [Marcy] It is.
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:27.514 --> 00:03:29.101
- [Marcy] Yeah, there's significant need.

00:03:29.101 --> 00:03:30.360
There are a lot of
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.357
- siblings, whether it's
two or more kids together,

00:03:32.357 --> 00:03:34.236
that's a big need in
the foster care space.

00:03:34.236 --> 00:03:37.323
And so I started blogging
about our experience

00:03:37.323 --> 00:03:39.820
through what kind of is a
complicated, difficult process.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.437
And that's what led to the organization

00:03:41.437 --> 00:03:42.469
that I founded today.

00:03:42.469 --> 00:03:43.670
- It's a very beautiful thing.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:46.259
Well Ariann, you have
something to tell Marcy, right?

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.217
- Yes.

00:03:47.217 --> 00:03:50.880
So Marcy we fully support what
you're doing and your mission

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.181
and you really have made
the impossible possible

00:03:55.181 --> 00:03:56.888
for so many children.

00:03:56.888 --> 00:03:58.884
And you know, just like the G2 pen,

00:03:58.884 --> 00:04:01.952
longest writing, unstoppable-
you are unstoppable.

00:04:01.952 --> 00:04:04.306
So we wanna offer you all the G2 pens

00:04:04.306 --> 00:04:07.238
and writing instruments
that you need for yourself

00:04:07.238 --> 00:04:09.177
and all the families
that you are working with

00:04:09.177 --> 00:04:11.487
through the adoption process.

00:04:11.487 --> 00:04:12.374
- Incredible.

00:04:12.374 --> 00:04:15.374
(audience cheering)

00:04:18.082 --> 00:04:19.586
- Well, actually there is one more thing

00:04:19.586 --> 00:04:20.769
I wanted to tell you.

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:24.544
And that is, you are not just a finalist

00:04:24.544 --> 00:04:26.750
for the G2 Overachievers grant.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:31.403
You are in fact, the G2
Overachievers grant winner.

00:04:31.403 --> 00:04:34.275
(audience cheering)

00:04:34.275 --> 00:04:37.016
- Woo! That's one
hundred thousand dollars.

00:04:37.016 --> 00:04:40.016
(audience cheering)

00:04:50.625 --> 00:04:52.176
That's so cool.

00:04:52.176 --> 00:04:55.531
Ah, well, here's some good news.

00:04:55.531 --> 00:04:57.902
Marcy is today's a hundred thousand dollar

00:04:57.902 --> 00:05:01.914
G2 Overachievers grant
winner but you can be next.

00:05:01.914 --> 00:05:04.826
Pilot pen is once again
looking for adults and students

00:05:04.826 --> 00:05:07.588
to go above and beyond
to make their communities

00:05:07.588 --> 00:05:09.690
and the whole world better for us all.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:12.085
That is why Pilot's hosting
the hundred thousand dollar

00:05:12.085 --> 00:05:13.879
G2 Overachievers grant

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:17.254
and the $15,000 G2
Overachievers student grant.

00:05:17.254 --> 00:05:19.352
They both go to outstanding overachievers

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:22.184
who go all out to improve
the lives of others.

00:05:22.184 --> 00:05:25.819
Submissions for the 2023
G2 Overachievers grants

00:05:25.819 --> 00:05:26.829
are open right now.

00:05:26.829 --> 00:05:28.154
So don't wait too long y'all.

00:05:28.154 --> 00:05:30.878
All submissions are due by December 15th.

00:05:30.878 --> 00:05:34.390
Find out how to apply
at g2overachievers.com.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:35.375
Stay right here, everybody

00:05:35.375 --> 00:05:36.558
I'll tell you what I'm liking next.

